course: dictionary
lesson: 11515
title: Alertness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Alertness is being awake, watchful and ready to notice things and react quickly. Someone with alertness spots danger early and acts fast. «The driver's alertness stopped the car just in time.» The driver was watching the road and reacted quickly, so alertness means being sharp and ready.
explain: The word comes from alert, which means awake and watching. Alertness is the noun, the state of being alert. You can have alertness, stay alert, or increase alertness. «Crossing the road needs full alertness: look, listen and think.»
explain: Look at the clue words around it. Words like watchful, ready and react show the meaning. If you swap in "being awake and ready to react", the sentence still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Alertness means being awake, watchful and ready to notice and react quickly.
fact: Alert is the adjective: «Stay alert when you cross the road.»
fact: Alertness is an uncountable noun, so we do not say "alertnesses".
fact: «Good sleep and a healthy breakfast help your alertness at school.»
fact: Useful phrases: mental alertness, stay alert, increase alertness.
exercise: «The driver's alertness stopped the car just in time.» What does alertness mean here? | *Being awake, watchful and ready to react | Feeling very sleepy and slow | Being lost on a road | Driving very fast
exercise: Which of these helps your alertness at school? | Watching TV in the dark | *Good sleep and a healthy breakfast | Skipping breakfast to save time | Staying up very late every night
exercise: Mia says, «Stay alert when you cross the road.» What should she do? | *Look, listen and watch for cars | Read a book while she walks | Close her eyes and walk quickly | Run across without looking
test: «Some people drink tea to increase their alertness before a test.» What does increase alertness mean? | *Make yourself more awake and ready to react | Make yourself fall asleep | Forget everything you learned | Make the test easier
test: Which word is the adjective form of alertness? | alarm | alertness | *alert | sleepy
exam: What is a good way to increase alertness before a long lesson? | Stay up all night playing games | Sleep through the whole morning | Skip lunch and sit very still | *Eat a healthy breakfast and get enough sleep
